      say: `Lab 1 needs PowerShell 7 with Pester, and no domain. Step 1 runs the standard's checks on the fixtures: five requests, of which two pass; nine Active Directory accounts; eight register rows; a certification campaign; and a Defender for Identity list, each built to trip one or more rules. The summary says twenty-five findings, four warnings, three for information. Two Chapter 6 rows and one retriever entry. One certification overdue. One account a person may delete, and nothing deleted. Then one line per rule, and the manifest's hash.`,
      detail: `You need PowerShell 7.1 or later with Pester 5. Work in examples/non-person-identity. Step 1: ./Invoke-NpiGmsaStandard.ps1 -InputPath tests/fixtures/ch12/inputs -StandardPath tests/fixtures/ch12/standard.json -OutputPath out/msa-standard -AsOf 2026-11-20. Expected: the summary, then one line per rule, then the manifest's SHA-256. As of 2026-11-20; 5 request(s), 9 AD managed account(s), 8 register row(s). Findings: 25 Finding, 4 Warn, 3 Info. Requests: 2 passed (REQ-2026-0201, REQ-2026-0202); 3 held. Chapter 06 inputs: 2 kerberos-replatform.csv row(s), 1 password-retrievers.json gMSA(s). Certification: 1 Current, 2 DueSoon, 1 Overdue; 2 ServiceNow finding(s). Retirement: 1 DeleteCandidate, 1 EnabledInAd, 1 SignInSinceDisable, 1 Wait; nothing deleted. Manifest SHA-256: 12ef8d960e8c8d618215f13c007f5d597f3cfda7b6fc60b6b0f8057311b9522d. The fixtures are fictional.`,
