      sources: "Sources: examples/non-person-identity fixtures (fictional). Chapter 12, “Lab 1: fixtures, no domain,” steps 4–7.",
      say: `Step 4 reads the certifications. The account gmsa print is overdue: it's in the lowest risk tier and was last certified in October 2025, and its owner revoked it, so it becomes a ServiceNow stale access finding. Step 5 is the retirement list. Only gmsa legacy may be deleted, and only by a person through the decommission ticket. Another account signed in after it was disabled, and a third is still enabled in Active Directory. Step 6 reads the evidence: one row per step and control, with its K S I's and the file's hash. Step 7 runs the tests: twenty-seven pass.`,
      detail: `Step 4, read the certifications and the ServiceNow findings: Get-Content out/msa-standard/certification.json -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json | Format-Table Account, RiskTier, LastCertifiedOn, DueOn, Status; Get-Content out/msa-standard/servicenow-findings.json -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json | Format-Table drift_class, severity, account_name, attribute, observed_value. gmsa-print$ is overdue (R3, last certified October 2025) and its owner revoked it, so it becomes a stale_access finding. Step 5, read the retirement list: Import-Csv out/msa-standard/retirement-list.csv | Format-Table SamAccountName, DisabledOn, LastLogon, DaysDisabled, Status. Only gmsa-legacy$ may be deleted (DeleteCandidate, 111 days disabled), and only by a person through the decommission ticket: gmsa-batch$ signed in after it was disabled (SignInSinceDisable), and gmsa-report$ is still enabled in Active Directory (EnabledInAd); gmsa-oldfax$ is Wait (50 days). Step 6, read the evidence: one row per step and control, with the KSIs aligned with it and the SHA-256 of the file that provides the evidence. Step 7, run the tests: Invoke-Pester -Path tests/NpiGmsaStandard.Tests.ps1; expected Tests Passed: 27, Failed: 0. After the steps: Remove-Item -Recurse -Force out.`,
