      sources: "Sources: SailPoint, AD connector; Learn, Defender for Identity service accounts; Get-ADServiceAccount. Chapter 12, “Lab 2: test domain and exports.”",
      say: `Lab 2 uses a test domain, never production, with Chapter 6's second lab already done, a SailPoint sandbox scoped to the service account unit, and Defender for Identity on the domain. The authors haven't run it. Write the test domain's settings. Then put the real exports into the kit's formats, mapping each product column by hand. Run with a live read of the domain; a group managed account you made by hand in Chapter 6 with no request shows up as finding eighteen, which is the drift rule working. Finally, confirm the manifest shows one read of Active Directory, and nothing else.`,
      detail: `Use a test Active Directory domain, never production, with Chapter 06's Lab 2 already done (a KDS root key, <service-account-ou>, the delegated DL-gMSA-Creators and at least one gMSA), a SailPoint sandbox with an Active Directory source scoped to <service-account-ou>, and Defender for Identity on the test domain. Lab 2 has not been run by the authors. Values you supply: <test-domain> (its DNS name), <dc> (a domain controller), <service-account-ou>, <groups-ou>, and <exports> (a folder for this lab's input files). Step 1: write the test domain's standard settings (standard.json with domain, serviceAccountOu, groupOu). Step 2: copy each fixture's header row (sailpoint-accounts, msa-register, certification-decisions, mdi-service-accounts) and a sample request, then add the test domain's rows from SailPoint's request and account exports, your register and Defender for Identity's Service Accounts page (Identities, then Service accounts, then Export), mapping each product column to the kit's column by hand; every request needs the fields Step 1 of Lab 1 showed. Step 3: ./Invoke-NpiGmsaStandard.ps1 -InputPath <exports> -StandardPath <exports>/standard.json -OutputPath out/msa-standard-test -Server <dc>; -Server replaces the fixture's ad-managed-accounts.json with Get-ADServiceAccount against <dc>, recorded in the manifest. Expected: the summary as in Lab 1 for the test domain's accounts; a gMSA created by hand in Chapter 06's Lab 2 with no request in the register is NPI-STD-18, the drift rule working. Step 4: read the live findings and the manifest's requests; expected one READ of Get-ADServiceAccount, and nothing else. After the steps: Remove-Item -Recurse -Force out.`,
